NOT READY — 2 blockers:
  ✗ Public address: NEXTAUTH_URL still points at localhost.
      → Set it to the site's public https:// address. Sign-in links, share cards, the feed and the sitemap are built from it.
  ✗ Email: No email provider: every verification link and password reset would be written to a log file and never delivered. Nobody could recover an account.
      → Set RESEND_API_KEY and EMAIL_FROM (docs/deployment.md §7).
6 warnings (the site works, but should not stay this way):
  ! Object storage: Uploads are stored on this server's disk. They are not backed up with the database and do not survive rebuilding the server.
      → Set S3_* and MEDIA_PUBLIC_BASE_URL (Cloudflare R2 or any S3-compatible bucket).
  ! Rate limiting: Rate limits are counted in this process only. Correct on one instance; on more than one, every limit is multiplied by the instance count.
      → Set UPSTASH_REDIS_REST_URL and UPSTASH_REDIS_REST_TOKEN before running more than one instance.
  ! Registration CAPTCHA: Registration has no CAPTCHA, so bots can create accounts at the rate limit.
      → Set NEXT_PUBLIC_TURNSTILE_SITE_KEY and TURNSTILE_SECRET_KEY (Cloudflare Turnstile, free).
  ! Malware scanning: Uploads are not malware-scanned. Every file is still re-encoded, which is the main control.
      → Run ClamAV (docker-compose ships it) and set CLAMAV_HOST.
  ! Phone verification: Verification texts are written to a log file; readers cannot verify a phone number.
      → Set TWILIO_ACCOUNT_SID, TWILIO_AUTH_TOKEN and TWILIO_FROM, or leave phone verification unused.
  ! Legal pages: The privacy policy and terms show placeholders: LEGAL_ENTITY, LEGAL_ADDRESS, LEGAL_CONTACT_EMAIL not set.
      → Set the LEGAL_* variables to the publishing entity's real details.
Configured: Database URL set, Auth secret set, ffmpeg for video and audio, Web push.

Fix the blockers above, or set ALLOW_PRODUCTION_FALLBACKS=1 on a staging server only.
